{"id": "EUVD-2026-104309", "enisaUuid": "e6b808a5-d05e-3cd3-8c80-f1e760b291f6", "description": "BentoML through 1.4.39 contains a Dockerfile instruction injection vulnerability that allows attackers to add arbitrary build instructions by embedding newlines in docker.env mapping keys rendered by the legacy base.j2 template. Attackers can supply a crafted bentofile.yaml or imported bento archive so that bentoml containerize executes injected RUN instructions during docker build, accessing build secrets and poisoning images.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:08:19", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/geo-chen/oss/blob/main/BentoML.md", "https://github.com/bentoml/BentoML/blob/v1.4.39/src/bentoml/_internal/container/frontend/dockerfile/templates/base.j2", "https://github.com/bentoml/BentoML/blob/v1.4.39/src/bentoml/_internal/bento/build_config.py", "https://github.com/bentoml/BentoML/blob/v1.4.39/src/bentoml/_internal/container/generate.py", "https://github.com/bentoml/BentoML/blob/v1.4.39/src/bentoml/_internal/container/__init__.py", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bentoml-through-1.4.39-dockerfile-instruction-injection-via-docker-env-keys"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112264", "GHSA-rq23-h86h-7v4x"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "64a37f33-a110-3469-864c-06e7cc25e416", "product": {"name": "BentoML", "vendor": {"name": "bentoml"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.4.39"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "319b5c29-268e-3a91-a0fd-eb412641d478", "vendor": {"name": "bentoml"}}], "isExploited": false}